+//! the studio runtime drops `SelectFileDialog`, and the Files a window manager
+//! runs may not be the person's own disk. A viewer reads the disk itself (its
+//! Left and Right walk the folder already), so it asks here: a sheet under its
+//! toolbar, over a dim that keeps the window in sight.
