+/// What is in front of the web views, as a frame draws it. A cover hides the readers below
+/// it: a higher `layer`, or the same layer and drawn before it. Layer 0 is the windows, in
+/// which what is drawn later is in front. Above them each of a shell's surfaces has a layer,
+/// in draw order, and those are over every window whenever they draw: a surface can draw
+/// before the windows and still lie over them, in an overlay list.
